# SABOTAGE: T80 (spec §I8 external enrichment provider seam) gate sabotage — defeats the
# FACADE-level FAIL-HONEST guard (ADR-014/024/026). `Samen.Enrichment.enrich/2` is the single
# chokepoint every enrich call routes through: it calls `provider_mod.configured?(config)` and
# returns `{:error, :not_configured}` IMMEDIATELY, without ever delegating to the provider, when
# the provider is not ready. This patch drops that guard entirely and delegates unconditionally
# to `provider_mod.enrich/3` — the exact "guard removed" shape as the canonical T74 mailbox
# sabotage (scripts/sabotages/58-t74-mailbox-fake-provider-canned-ok.patch), but applied at the
# layer that ACTUALLY enforces this guarantee for enrichment (the facade, not the fake — the
# fake's own `enrich/3` checks `capabilities()` BEFORE it ever reaches its own `configured?`
# guard, so with the facade guard removed and no capability declared, the call now returns
# `{:error, :not_implemented}` instead of `{:error, :not_configured}` — a genuine, non-vacuous
# assertion failure on the exact atom the fail-honest contract promises). Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/enrichment_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: unconfigured provider returns {:error, :not_configured}
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/enrichment.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/enrichment.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/enrichment.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/enrichment.ex
@@ -14,11 +14,7 @@
   def enrich(subject_type, subject_id) when subject_type in [:person, :company] do
     {provider_mod, config} = provider_selection()

-    if provider_mod.configured?(config) do
-      provider_mod.enrich(subject_type, subject_id, config)
-    else
-      {:error, :not_configured}
-    end
+    provider_mod.enrich(subject_type, subject_id, config)
   end

   @doc "Check if the enrichment provider is configured and ready."
